message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Erdős Problem #616: t(21) = 4 — paper, Lean formalization, SAT encodings"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yong
    given-names: Jerry
    email: jerryjyong@gmail.com
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Erdős problems
  - hypergraphs
  - transversal number
  - computer-assisted proof
  - SAT
  - LRAT
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  For r >= 3 let t(r) be the largest transversal number of a finite r-uniform hypergraph in which every
  subhypergraph spanned by at most 3r-3 vertices has transversal number at most 1 (Erdős Problem #616).
  The Erdős–Hajnal–Tuza bounds leave t(21) in {4, 5}. This repository contains a computer-assisted proof
  that t(21) = 4: a paper, a Lean 4 formalization of the full argument against the formal-conjectures
  statement, and the SAT encodings, generators and independent re-encodings of its four computational
  leaves. The certificates (CNF/DRAT/LRAT) are distributed as a release asset.
